{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0416a655-6d43-4be9-9191-ad960d656524","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have completed the task and built `lab-18-transactions` according to the requested scope. \n\nHere is a summary of the work:\n1. **Created Simulations**: \n   - Wrote `wal_shadow.c` to benchmark and compare commit latencies between Write-Ahead Logging (1 synchronous write) and Shadow Paging (2 synchronous writes) using `clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC)` in the VM.\n   - Wrote `quicksilver_2pc.py` in Python 3.12 to simulate a Quicksilver-style transaction tree, demonstrating normal two-phase commits, voting aborts on node timeouts, and coordinator crash/recovery.\n2. **Setup Lab Tooling**:\n   - Created the `Makefile` with `all`, `run`, `test`, and `clean` targets.\n   - Fixed C compiler warnings and verified that tests pass under `run-in-vm.sh labs/lab-18-transactions test`.\n   - Captured the realistic `expected-output.txt` from the Lima VM.\n   - Added a `.gitignore` to omit binaries.\n3. **Drafted the README**: \n   - Wrote the `README.md` following the strict CI guidelines (one sentence per line, no emojis, strict ASCII punctuation).\n   - Filled out the goals, prerequisites, running commands, and expected output text.\n   - Designed 3 predictive experiments focused on caching (`fdatasync`), tree depths, and subordinate crash recovery.\n   - Detailed 4 conceptual review questions with folded answers based on the L08c notes.\n4. **Commits and Hand-off**:\n   - Successfully staged and committed the files on `aos/writer-part-0-1`.\n   - Wrote the final supervisor report detailing the work to `/Users/shreejitverma/github/career-ops/library/01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/CS6210-AOS/crew/runner/reports/lab-18-transactions.md`.\n\nNo human intervention is needed, the lab status is set to `solid` and ready for the supervisor to integrate.\n","duration_seconds":177.938855,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":127204,"output_tokens":16055,"thinking_tokens":5845,"cache_read_tokens":911340,"total_tokens":143259}}}
